          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
            ],
            "text/markdown": "| ML Model Name | Observation about model performance |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Logistic Regression** | A linear model on scaled and one-hot inputs: fast, stable and well calibrated, but it cannot model non-linear interactions between features. Test accuracy 0.583 (rank 2 of 5; majority-class baseline 0.539), AUC 0.672, F1 0.529, MCC 0.197 (rank 2). Fit check: consistent generalisation (train-test accuracy gap 0.003). Recall for the minority class '<30' is 0.021. |\n| **Decision Tree** | A single depth-limited tree: easy to interpret and able to capture non-linear splits, but a single tree is high-variance. Test accuracy 0.573 (rank 3 of 5; majority-class baseline 0.539), AUC 0.643, F1 0.516, MCC 0.173 (rank 3). Fit check: consistent generalisation (train-test accuracy gap 0.011). Recall for the minority class '<30' is 0.011. |\n| **kNN** | Distance based on 205 encoded features: distances become less informative in high dimensions, and prediction is slow on a large test set. Test accuracy 0.533 (rank 4 of 5; majority-class baseline 0.539), AUC 0.596, F1 0.511, MCC 0.137 (rank 4). Fit check: clear overfitting (train-test accuracy gap 0.123). Recall for the minority class '<30' is 0.076. |\n| **Naive Bayes** | Assumes features are independent and Gaussian; the one-hot and medication features are correlated and not Gaussian, so the assumptions are violated. Test accuracy 0.165 (rank 5 of 5; majority-class baseline 0.539), AUC 0.587, F1 0.130, MCC 0.067 (rank 5). Fit check: consistent generalisation (train-test accuracy gap 0.003). Recall for the minority class '<30' is 0.948. |\n| **Random Forest (Ensemble)** | Averages many de-correlated trees, which reduces variance and captures non-linear interactions. Test accuracy 0.591 (rank 1 of 5; majority-class baseline 0.539), AUC 0.679, F1 0.537, MCC 0.214 (rank 1). Fit check: clear overfitting (train-test accuracy gap 0.310). Recall for the minority class '<30' is 0.009. |\n| **Overall Winner for your dataset?** | **Random Forest (Ensemble)** is the overall winner: it has the highest MCC (0.214), which is the most reliable single score on an imbalanced multi-class target, and it is best on 6 of the 6 metrics (best per metric: Accuracy: Random Forest (Ensemble), AUC: Random Forest (Ensemble), Precision: Random Forest (Ensemble), Recall: Random Forest (Ensemble), F1: Random Forest (Ensemble), MCC: Random Forest (Ensemble)). Its AUC is 0.679 and its train-test accuracy gap is 0.310. |"
          },
